Reference ingredients and traditional-use context

[P00342 | 30127:30133 | NORMAL_TEXT | TABLE row=1 col=0]
Colds

[P00343 | 30134:30136 | NORMAL_TEXT | TABLE row=1 col=1]
[INLINE_OBJECT kix.o96nzb24wyo4]

[P00344 | 30136:30159 | NORMAL_TEXT | TABLE row=1 col=1]
Yin Qiao type remedies

[P00345 | 30160:30532 | NORMAL_TEXT | TABLE row=1 col=2]
Mei Hua Yin Qiao contains honeysuckle, forsythia, platycodon, mint, lophatherum, licorice, schizonepeta, prepared soybean, burdock fruit and reed rhizome. [Science Arts](https://www.sciencearts.com/shop/yin-qiao-capsules-30-s) describes a heat-related presentation involving fever, sore throat and thirst, with tongue and pulse features also listed. These are reference descriptors for comparison with the broad complaint “colds”.

[P00346 | 30534:30544 | NORMAL_TEXT | TABLE row=2 col=0]
Diarrhoea

[P00347 | 30545:30547 | NORMAL_TEXT | TABLE row=2 col=1]
[INLINE_OBJECT kix.t7vqzv1xb9pw]

[P00348 | 30547:30578 | NORMAL_TEXT | TABLE row=2 col=1]
Huoxiang Zhengqi type remedies

[P00349 | 30579:30988 | NORMAL_TEXT | TABLE row=2 col=2]
Mei Hua Huoxiang Zhengqi contains patchouli, perilla leaf, angelica dahurica root, atractylodes, tangerine peel, pinellia, magnolia bark, poria, platycodon, licorice, areca peel, jujube and ginger. [Science Arts](https://www.sciencearts.com/shop/condensed-huoxiang-zhengqi-wan-200-s) describes dampness-related presentations involving vomiting, diarrhoea, abdominal fullness and body heaviness. The reference context distinguishes a symptom cluster from diarrhoea considered alone.

[P00350 | 30990:31024 | NORMAL_TEXT | TABLE row=3 col=0]
Fatigue or Qi deficiency language

[P00351 | 31025:31027 | NORMAL_TEXT | TABLE row=3 col=1]
[INLINE_OBJECT kix.wtt1e2tyu2k]

[P00352 | 31027:31048 | NORMAL_TEXT | TABLE row=3 col=1]
Ginseng or Dang Shen

[P00353 | 31049:31403 | NORMAL_TEXT | TABLE row=3 col=2]
Ginseng and Dang Shen are separate Qi-tonifying materials rather than one fixed formula. PolyU describes [ginseng](https://herbaltcm.sn.polyu.edu.hk/herbal/ginseng) as supporting original Qi and Spleen–Lung functions, and [Dang Shen](https://herbaltcm.sn.polyu.edu.hk/herbal/tangshen) as supporting Spleen and Lung Qi. Reference symptoms include poor appetite, shortness of breath and, for Dang Shen, loose stools; these provide context beyond fatigue alone.

[P00354 | 31405:31430 | NORMAL_TEXT | TABLE row=4 col=0]
Perceived lower immunity

[P00355 | 31431:31433 | NORMAL_TEXT | TABLE row=4 col=1]
[INLINE_OBJECT kix.ny8u73434gzc]

[P00356 | 31433:31456 | NORMAL_TEXT | TABLE row=4 col=1]
Lingzhi or supplements

[P00357 | 31457:31800 | NORMAL_TEXT | TABLE row=4 col=2]
Reference Lingzhi is the dried fruiting body of Ganoderma lucidum or G. sinense. [PolyU](https://herbaltcm.sn.polyu.edu.hk/herbal/glossy-ganoderma) describes traditional Qi-tonifying and calming uses, with reference symptoms including insomnia, palpitations and shortness of breath. “Lower immunity” is a broad retail description and does not specify a single formula, TCM pattern or clinical diagnosis.

[P00358 | 31802:31842 | NORMAL_TEXT | TABLE row=5 col=0]
Late nights, stress and long work hours

[P00359 | 31843:31845 | NORMAL_TEXT | TABLE row=5 col=1]
[INLINE_OBJECT kix.4d7d05ly06h]

[P00360 | 31845:31881 | NORMAL_TEXT | TABLE row=5 col=1]
Liver care or mood support products

[P00361 | 31882:32265 | NORMAL_TEXT | TABLE row=5 col=2]
Mind Soothe is a 16-ingredient example; key ingredients listed by [Tong Jum Chew](https://tongjumchew.com/product/natures-green-mind-soothe-capsules-60s/) include bupleurum, acorus, lily bulb, sour jujube seed, curcuma, polygala, licorice and jujube. The manufacturer describes Liver-constraint and restlessness-related uses. Its reference symptom context includes sleep and mood concerns; late nights or long work hours alone do not establish that pattern.

[P00362 | 32267:32285 | NORMAL_TEXT | TABLE row=6 col=0]
Aches or injuries

[P00363 | 32286:32288 | NORMAL_TEXT | TABLE row=6 col=1]
[INLINE_OBJECT kix.bv9pp2j4h4zb]

[P00364 | 32288:32303 | NORMAL_TEXT | TABLE row=6 col=1]
Medicated oils

[P00365 | 32304:32679 | NORMAL_TEXT | TABLE row=6 col=2]
Reference [Fei Fah Red Flower Ointment](https://feifah.com/products/red-flower-ointment-50ml) is an external liniment containing methyl salicylate, turpentine, white oil and menthol among its listed ingredients. Fei Fah describes use for sprains, bruises and muscular aches. This identifies the illustrated product’s composition and intended use; the general category “medicated oils” includes products